1
00:00:21,897 --> 00:00:23,731
Oh, okay.

2
00:00:23,815 --> 00:00:25,567
Where are we now?

3
00:00:25,651 --> 00:00:27,569
Got the VRI for our
deaf patient in Central 12.

4
00:00:27,653 --> 00:00:29,653
Still waiting on Pedes
for Baby Jane Doe.

5
00:00:29,655 --> 00:00:31,531
Central six is sitting pretty
with his insulin drip.

6
00:00:31,615 --> 00:00:33,074
And the Westbridge
diversions are

7
00:00:33,158 --> 00:00:34,409
kindly waiting
their turn to sit

8
00:00:34,493 --> 00:00:35,993
for hours in our lovely halls.

9
00:00:36,036 --> 00:00:37,912
You are some kind of savant.

10
00:00:37,996 --> 00:00:38,996
Worthy of a raise?

11
00:00:39,039 --> 00:00:40,832
Just more of my love.

12
00:00:40,916 --> 00:00:42,292
I got enough of that.

13
00:00:42,376 --> 00:00:44,627
I have a sexual
assault victim in triage.

14
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:46,921
I called PAAR,
so an advocate is on the way.

15
00:00:47,005 --> 00:00:49,257
Okay. We'll take care of it.

16
00:00:49,341 --> 00:00:52,093
Uh, Dr. McKay, what's going on
with your patient in Central nine?

17
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:53,470
Isn't she good to go?

18
00:00:53,554 --> 00:00:55,263
Oh, she was, but she decided

19
00:00:55,347 --> 00:00:56,764
she wanted to stay
in the hospital now

20
00:00:56,848 --> 00:00:58,099
because she's in too much pain.

21
00:00:58,183 --> 00:01:00,059
In our loud
and overcrowded ED

22
00:01:00,143 --> 00:01:02,270
with more Westbridge cases
arriving every moment?

23
00:01:02,354 --> 00:01:04,230
She would be
more comfortable at home.

24
00:01:04,314 --> 00:01:07,609
The debrief was lovely.

25
00:01:07,693 --> 00:01:09,402
Thank you.

26
00:01:09,486 --> 00:01:11,279
Would you mind helping Dana
with a sexual assault victim

27
00:01:11,363 --> 00:01:13,281
who just came in?
- Of course. Sure.

28
00:01:13,365 --> 00:01:15,116
Why don't you and I go
see if we can't convince

29
00:01:15,200 --> 00:01:16,900
your patient to leave?
- All right.

30
00:01:16,952 --> 00:01:19,496
I need to take care of a sexual
assault victim in triage.

31
00:01:19,580 --> 00:01:21,289
One of you needs
to hold down the fort.

32
00:01:21,373 --> 00:01:23,958
- We can call for a SANE.
- On a holiday? Could be hours.

33
00:01:24,042 --> 00:01:25,668
We're not gonna make
this patient wait.

34
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:26,794
And since I'm the only
SANE on staff--

35
00:01:26,878 --> 00:01:28,171
Princess will cover.

36
00:01:28,255 --> 00:01:29,964
[Speaking Tagalog]

37
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:31,799
Hey! Hey!

38
00:01:31,883 --> 00:01:33,301
You two better not be
teaching her any bad habits.

39
00:01:33,385 --> 00:01:35,929
Come on. You ready, Doc?
- Sure.

40
00:01:36,013 --> 00:01:38,806
A SANE is a Sexual Assault
Nurse Examiner.

41
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:41,017
We do forensic exams,
collect evidence,

42
00:01:41,101 --> 00:01:43,686
and hand it over to the police
if a report is made.

43
00:01:43,770 --> 00:01:45,688
We also provide
resources, support,

44
00:01:45,772 --> 00:01:48,066
sometimes even testimony.
- You go to court?

45
00:01:48,150 --> 00:01:51,000
SANEs are very valuable in
a hospital, especially an ED.

46
00:01:51,069 --> 00:01:52,862
More nurses should
train for it.

47
00:01:52,946 --> 00:01:54,948
That's a not so subtle hint.

48
00:01:56,575 --> 00:01:58,993
[Phone ringing]

49
00:01:59,077 --> 00:02:02,331
[indistinct conversations]

50
00:02:03,248 --> 00:02:05,291
Looks like this is
the new hot spot, huh?

51
00:02:05,375 --> 00:02:06,834
And only getting hotter.

52
00:02:06,918 --> 00:02:08,670
Any word on what's
going on with Westbridge?

53
00:02:08,754 --> 00:02:10,054
I got 20 on lantern flies.

54
00:02:10,088 --> 00:02:12,298
Nope, nothing.

55
00:02:12,382 --> 00:02:15,552
These patient passports have
an interesting alternative use.

56
00:02:15,636 --> 00:02:17,011
Where's the sexual
assault victim?

57
00:02:17,095 --> 00:02:18,513
She's in Triage, Chair two.

58
00:02:18,597 --> 00:02:20,515
Thanks, Lupe.

59
00:02:20,599 --> 00:02:21,599
Here's her intake.

60
00:02:21,600 --> 00:02:23,518
Got it.

61
00:02:23,602 --> 00:02:25,646
[Sighs]

62
00:02:29,941 --> 00:02:31,859
Hi, Ms. Miller.

63
00:02:31,943 --> 00:02:33,194
I'm Dana.

64
00:02:33,278 --> 00:02:34,862
How are you doing?

65
00:02:34,946 --> 00:02:37,407
- I've been better.
- Yeah.

66
00:02:37,491 --> 00:02:38,866
You're in a safe place now.

67
00:02:38,950 --> 00:02:40,702
I'm the charge nurse in the ED

68
00:02:40,786 --> 00:02:42,912
and a sexual assault
nurse examiner.

69
00:02:42,996 --> 00:02:44,539
This is Emma,
who will be assisting.

70
00:02:44,623 --> 00:02:46,082
And I'm Dr. Al-Hashimi.

71
00:02:46,166 --> 00:02:47,458
I'll be checking you
for any injuries

72
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:50,128
that need immediate attention.

73
00:02:50,212 --> 00:02:52,046
You can just call me Ilana.

74
00:02:52,130 --> 00:02:53,430
I don't have any injuries.

75
00:02:53,465 --> 00:02:55,091
Okay, that's good.

76
00:02:55,175 --> 00:02:56,968
We're gonna get
a room ready for you.

77
00:02:57,052 --> 00:02:58,928
Meanwhile, Dr. Al-Hashimi is
gonna ask you a few questions.

78
00:02:59,012 --> 00:03:01,055
How long is this gonna take?

79
00:03:01,139 --> 00:03:02,724
I can't promise
an exact time,

80
00:03:02,808 --> 00:03:05,602
but we'll try to be
as fast as you need.

81
00:03:05,686 --> 00:03:07,020
- Thank you.
- Yeah.

82
00:03:11,274 --> 00:03:14,402
Okay, Ilana, do you take any
prescription medications?

83
00:03:14,486 --> 00:03:16,446
Just Synthroid,
one tab a day.

84
00:03:16,530 --> 00:03:18,281
Okay, and any allergies
to medications?

85
00:03:18,365 --> 00:03:20,491
- No. No.
- Okay.

86
00:03:20,575 --> 00:03:22,493
Dana will come get you
when the room is ready,

87
00:03:22,577 --> 00:03:24,705
and I'll be back
to finish your exam.

88
00:03:31,837 --> 00:03:33,129
Come find me
when she's in a gown.

89
00:03:33,213 --> 00:03:34,881
Will do.

90
00:03:34,965 --> 00:03:36,758
We're gonna use Triage Exam
Rooms one and two for this.

91
00:03:36,842 --> 00:03:39,636
It's the most private space
we have away from the ED.

92
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:41,387
All right, this can be a lot.

93
00:03:41,471 --> 00:03:43,264
You up for it?

94
00:03:43,348 --> 00:03:44,474
Yeah.

95
00:03:44,558 --> 00:03:46,309
Yes. I'm good.

96
00:03:46,393 --> 00:03:48,603
Let me know if
you need to step out.

97
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:57,446
[Sighs] Yes.

98
00:03:59,698 --> 00:04:01,324
Dr. Ellis.

99
00:04:01,408 --> 00:04:03,451
- Oh, no.
- Oh, yes.

100
00:04:03,535 --> 00:04:04,786
Need the room.

101
00:04:04,870 --> 00:04:06,788
Find another place
to lay your head.

102
00:04:06,872 --> 00:04:09,457
Not even
a 20-minute power nap?

103
00:04:09,541 --> 00:04:11,084
You know, my double is at 1:30.
I'm--

104
00:04:11,168 --> 00:04:12,960
Nope, we're getting
Westbridge diversions.

105
00:04:13,044 --> 00:04:14,253
And chairs is insane.

106
00:04:14,337 --> 00:04:15,755
Did you see out there?
- No.

107
00:04:15,839 --> 00:04:17,340
I do not come in
through that mess.

108
00:04:17,424 --> 00:04:19,050
Okay.

109
00:04:19,134 --> 00:04:20,343
Yeah.

110
00:04:20,427 --> 00:04:21,969
People sleep in here?

111
00:04:22,053 --> 00:04:24,203
Yeah, the night shift docs
just need rest,

112
00:04:24,222 --> 00:04:25,973
especially if they have to
come in during the day.

113
00:04:26,057 --> 00:04:28,226
But today, we can't
waste the space.

114
00:04:28,310 --> 00:04:33,315
I need you to get me a stool on
wheels and Esme for a turnover.

115
00:04:36,443 --> 00:04:39,738
So you're having a headache
and abdominal pain?

116
00:04:43,408 --> 00:04:45,201
<i>Yeah, that's right.</i>

117
00:04:45,285 --> 00:04:47,829
Okay, and which would
you say is worse?

118
00:04:51,416 --> 00:04:53,209
<i>My headache was terrible
last week...</i>

119
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:56,170
<i>[Voice distorting]
But now--[static crackles]</i>

120
00:04:56,254 --> 00:04:57,338
- Hey, you're--
You're breaking up.

121
00:04:57,422 --> 00:04:58,881
Can you run that back again?

122
00:04:58,965 --> 00:05:00,508
<i>Sure.</i>

123
00:05:00,592 --> 00:05:03,511
[Clears throat]

124
00:05:03,595 --> 00:05:05,847
<i>My headache was terrible
last week...</i>

125
00:05:05,931 --> 00:05:09,183
<i>[Voice distorting]
But now my abdominal pain--</i>

126
00:05:09,267 --> 00:05:10,351
Oh, my God.

127
00:05:10,435 --> 00:05:12,311
Come on, you piece of--

128
00:05:12,395 --> 00:05:13,855
Fuck.

129
00:05:13,939 --> 00:05:15,315
Um--

130
00:05:41,174 --> 00:05:43,551
I'll--
- I'll be right back.

131
00:05:43,635 --> 00:05:45,387
Sorry.

132
00:05:51,643 --> 00:05:53,060
Um, Dr. Al-Hashimi?

133
00:05:53,144 --> 00:05:54,771
Jackson's parents are here.

134
00:05:54,855 --> 00:05:57,482
Okay. I'll take that.

135
00:05:57,566 --> 00:06:00,318
Um, Mr. and Mrs. Davis,
this is one of my attendings,

136
00:06:00,402 --> 00:06:02,487
Dr. Al-Hashimi.
- Hi. Nice to meet you.

137
00:06:02,571 --> 00:06:04,614
- Demi.
- Charles.

138
00:06:04,698 --> 00:06:06,449
What the hell's going on?

139
00:06:06,533 --> 00:06:08,534
He's barely conscious.

140
00:06:08,618 --> 00:06:10,203
Jackson's just a little tired
due to the sedative

141
00:06:10,287 --> 00:06:12,288
he was given.
- You sedated him?

142
00:06:12,372 --> 00:06:14,582
Oh, your son was brought in
extremely agitated.

143
00:06:14,666 --> 00:06:15,917
You'd be, too,
if you were tased.

144
00:06:16,001 --> 00:06:18,252
And why the fuck
did they do that?

145
00:06:18,336 --> 00:06:20,963
This is bullshit.
We're taking him home.

146
00:06:21,047 --> 00:06:22,883
Why don't we step out
for a second?

147
00:06:31,558 --> 00:06:34,811
Right now, Jackson is on
an involuntary psych hold.

148
00:06:34,895 --> 00:06:36,687
- What?
That's not necessary.

149
00:06:36,771 --> 00:06:38,147
He just needs some rest.

150
00:06:38,231 --> 00:06:40,066
He's been studying
for the bar exam.

151
00:06:40,150 --> 00:06:41,567
We can watch him at home.

152
00:06:41,651 --> 00:06:43,110
So far, all of his tests
look good,

153
00:06:43,194 --> 00:06:46,113
but Jackson has
reported hearing voices.

154
00:06:46,197 --> 00:06:47,824
This could be serious.

155
00:06:47,908 --> 00:06:49,951
Dr. Jefferson will come back
and speak with you.

156
00:06:50,035 --> 00:06:52,954
He can explain more of what
may be going on with Jackson.

157
00:06:53,038 --> 00:06:54,539
And who is Dr. Jefferson?

158
00:06:54,623 --> 00:06:56,582
He's from Psychiatry,
and he's excellent.

159
00:06:56,666 --> 00:06:58,793
He can explain next steps and
answer all of your questions.

160
00:06:58,877 --> 00:07:01,128
Javadi, why don't you take
the Davises to the family room?

161
00:07:01,212 --> 00:07:02,505
- Sure.
- Excuse me.

162
00:07:02,589 --> 00:07:03,965
It's just this way.

163
00:07:04,049 --> 00:07:06,968
<i>[Soft tense music]</i>

164
00:07:17,228 --> 00:07:18,980
[Sighs shakily]

165
00:07:22,901 --> 00:07:25,653
<i>[line trills]</i>

166
00:07:25,737 --> 00:07:28,239
<i>You have reached the
Pittsburgh Neuroscience Group.</i>

167
00:07:28,323 --> 00:07:30,199
<i>If this is
a medical emergency,</i>

168
00:07:30,283 --> 00:07:33,327
<i>please hang up and dial 911.</i>

169
00:07:33,411 --> 00:07:36,330
<i>For our address and
office hours, press one.</i>

170
00:07:36,414 --> 00:07:39,125
<i>To refill a prescription,
press two.</i>

171
00:07:39,209 --> 00:07:43,671
<i>To leave a message for
the doctor on call--</i>

172
00:07:43,755 --> 00:07:45,840
Hi, this is
Dr. Baran al-Hashimi.

173
00:07:45,924 --> 00:07:47,800
I'm a patient
of Dr. Fairgraves.

174
00:07:47,884 --> 00:07:51,721
I need to speak to him
if he's on call.

175
00:07:51,805 --> 00:07:54,974
If he's not, I'll take his
next available appointment.

176
00:07:55,058 --> 00:07:58,185
And please call me
if he has a cancellation.

177
00:07:58,269 --> 00:08:00,271
Thank you.

178
00:08:00,355 --> 00:08:02,732
Like I said, you're more than
welcome to stay down here

179
00:08:02,816 --> 00:08:04,567
until an inpatient bed
opens up upstairs.

180
00:08:04,651 --> 00:08:07,862
But that can take a while,
sometimes days,

181
00:08:07,946 --> 00:08:10,323
even longer.

182
00:08:10,407 --> 00:08:11,824
It's gonna be
really noisy here,

183
00:08:11,908 --> 00:08:13,367
and you won't get any rest.

184
00:08:13,451 --> 00:08:15,077
At home, you'll be
surrounded by your family

185
00:08:15,161 --> 00:08:18,581
and be more comfortable.

186
00:08:18,665 --> 00:08:20,792
It's your choice, Roxie.

187
00:08:23,086 --> 00:08:25,838
It's not that
I don't wanna go home, but--

188
00:08:25,922 --> 00:08:28,049
- Hi, Mom.
- Mom.

189
00:08:28,133 --> 00:08:31,719
- Lena texted me to come back.
I figured I'd bring the boys.

190
00:08:31,803 --> 00:08:34,221
What's going on?
Is everything okay?

191
00:08:34,305 --> 00:08:37,892
Robby, police officer,
incoming trauma.

192
00:08:37,976 --> 00:08:39,101
Coming.

193
00:08:39,185 --> 00:08:40,478
I'll be right back.

194
00:08:40,562 --> 00:08:42,112
We'll give you
a chance to talk.

195
00:08:44,649 --> 00:08:47,152
Okay, why don't you
have a seat?

196
00:08:55,035 --> 00:08:57,328
Do you need anything
before we begin?

197
00:09:02,292 --> 00:09:04,919
You're in control now, Ilana.

198
00:09:05,003 --> 00:09:07,713
We're here to help
and support you.

199
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:11,133
Once I open this kit,
I cannot leave the room.

200
00:09:11,217 --> 00:09:14,220
But if you need a break
or some air, just let us know.

201
00:09:14,304 --> 00:09:17,473
Okay? Emma can go
with you if you like.

202
00:09:17,557 --> 00:09:19,976
An advocate from
Pittsburgh Action Against Rape

203
00:09:20,060 --> 00:09:21,602
has been called,
and they should arrive soon.

204
00:09:21,686 --> 00:09:24,271
- Can we start?
- Sure.

205
00:09:24,355 --> 00:09:25,731
I'm gonna put my face shield on

206
00:09:25,815 --> 00:09:27,942
so I don't
contaminate anything.

207
00:09:28,026 --> 00:09:30,903
Emma has already done the same.

208
00:09:30,987 --> 00:09:34,865
Now, in order for the doctor
to do her exam,

209
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:36,450
I need you in a gown,

210
00:09:36,534 --> 00:09:37,660
but I need to collect
your clothing first.

211
00:09:37,744 --> 00:09:39,662
Is that okay?

212
00:09:43,750 --> 00:09:46,669
I'm gonna need you to undress
on top of these pads.

213
00:09:46,753 --> 00:09:49,630
Put each item of clothing
on the pads, okay?

214
00:09:49,714 --> 00:09:53,175
Then we'll package each piece
in a separate bag.

215
00:09:53,259 --> 00:09:54,343
We'll get you new clothes.

216
00:09:54,427 --> 00:09:55,720
Don't worry.
- All right.

217
00:09:55,804 --> 00:09:57,471
Emma's gonna be
behind this curtain,

218
00:09:57,555 --> 00:10:00,474
and I'll be in here with you.

219
00:10:00,558 --> 00:10:03,644
And take off your shoes first.

220
00:10:03,728 --> 00:10:07,982
When you're done,
I want you to put on your gown

221
00:10:08,066 --> 00:10:11,110
open in the back.

222
00:10:11,194 --> 00:10:14,280
[Breathing in]

223
00:10:35,468 --> 00:10:37,678
What if the mom
doesn't wanna leave?

224
00:10:37,762 --> 00:10:39,930
Well, then she's gonna
have to put up with us.

225
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:41,849
[Sighs]

226
00:10:41,933 --> 00:10:44,685
I can't imagine--her boys.

227
00:10:44,769 --> 00:10:46,520
Oh, don't go there.

228
00:10:46,604 --> 00:10:48,189
I'm gonna see if
I can grease the wheels,

229
00:10:48,273 --> 00:10:49,398
get her a room upstairs soon.

230
00:10:49,482 --> 00:10:51,358
- Good luck.
What was that?

231
00:10:51,442 --> 00:10:52,777
Battle plan
for our hall space.

232
00:10:52,861 --> 00:10:54,361
It's filling up fast.

233
00:10:54,445 --> 00:10:56,072
Police officer should
be here any minute.

234
00:10:56,156 --> 00:10:57,865
Yeah, well, as soon
as you can, please,

235
00:10:57,949 --> 00:10:59,249
I need you to fix the VRI.

236
00:10:59,284 --> 00:11:00,701
All right. Thanks.

237
00:11:00,785 --> 00:11:02,203
Santos, I need you
to pick up some more

238
00:11:02,287 --> 00:11:03,662
of these Westbridge diversions.
- Sure.

239
00:11:03,746 --> 00:11:05,164
You want my firstborn too?

240
00:11:05,248 --> 00:11:07,333
- Maybe.
Will they know how to suture?

241
00:11:07,417 --> 00:11:09,001
Intubated neck wound,
sats not great.

242
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:11,003
We were diverted here.
Is there a trauma room open?

243
00:11:11,087 --> 00:11:12,755
- Trauma one!
- What's the story?

244
00:11:12,839 --> 00:11:15,341
My buddy, Officer Hiro,
high-velocity GSW.

245
00:11:15,425 --> 00:11:16,775
He's getting harder to bag.

246
00:11:16,801 --> 00:11:19,512
Warehouse robbery
gone sideways.

247
00:11:19,596 --> 00:11:20,679
One, two, three.

248
00:11:20,763 --> 00:11:22,181
You guys wait here.

249
00:11:22,265 --> 00:11:23,933
We'll take care of him,
I promise.

250
00:11:24,017 --> 00:11:25,601
I thought you left us
already for the open road?

251
00:11:25,685 --> 00:11:27,285
And miss seeing you
in uniform?

252
00:11:27,312 --> 00:11:29,063
You should see me
as a flight attendant.

253
00:11:29,147 --> 00:11:31,107
- Did you do this intubation?
- Under active fire, yeah.

254
00:11:31,191 --> 00:11:32,858
Are you serious?

255
00:11:32,942 --> 00:11:34,318
I go in with the team
in case there's an injury.

256
00:11:34,402 --> 00:11:35,945
That's badass.

257
00:11:36,029 --> 00:11:37,613
Dr. Santos, let's make sure
these lungs are up.

258
00:11:37,697 --> 00:11:39,365
Could you see the cords?
- Yeah, there was a great view,

259
00:11:39,449 --> 00:11:40,991
but it was hard to pass
after I cleared them.

260
00:11:41,075 --> 00:11:42,952
Yeah, sats down to 85.

261
00:11:43,036 --> 00:11:44,912
Dr. Santos, what could
cause respiratory failure

262
00:11:44,996 --> 00:11:46,580
in an intubated patient?

263
00:11:46,664 --> 00:11:47,790
There are a lot
of possibilities.

264
00:11:47,874 --> 00:11:49,333
Think DOPE.

265
00:11:49,417 --> 00:11:51,585
Displacement, Obstruction,
Pneumothorax,

266
00:11:51,669 --> 00:11:52,962
Equipment failure.

267
00:11:53,046 --> 00:11:55,464
Good lung sliding, no pneumo.

268
00:11:55,548 --> 00:11:57,091
It is displacement.

269
00:11:57,175 --> 00:11:59,510
Okay, that is
a transected trachea.

270
00:11:59,594 --> 00:12:01,428
[Grunting]

271
00:12:01,512 --> 00:12:03,472
Pulling out.

272
00:12:03,556 --> 00:12:05,266
Bag.

273
00:12:05,350 --> 00:12:06,642
But if you intubate again,
won't it just come straight

274
00:12:06,726 --> 00:12:08,176
out the wound?
- Yep, exactly.

275
00:12:08,186 --> 00:12:09,436
So we're gonna
need another plan.

276
00:12:09,520 --> 00:12:11,272
Okay. Sats down to 83.

277
00:12:11,356 --> 00:12:12,731
Yeah, he's not
moving any air.

278
00:12:12,815 --> 00:12:14,608
Okay, I need a neonatal mask.

279
00:12:14,692 --> 00:12:17,236
- Neonatal?
- Yep.

280
00:12:17,320 --> 00:12:19,738
I'm just going to finish
my initial exam.

281
00:12:19,822 --> 00:12:21,741
Let me know if you
feel any pain, okay?

282
00:12:25,703 --> 00:12:28,289
My legs are fine.

283
00:12:28,373 --> 00:12:29,999
All looks good.

284
00:12:30,083 --> 00:12:32,418
No need for X-rays
or advanced imaging.

285
00:12:32,502 --> 00:12:34,003
Got it.

286
00:12:34,087 --> 00:12:36,463
- Two areas of ecchymosis...
- That means bruising.

287
00:12:36,547 --> 00:12:38,174
Over the shoulders
bilaterally.

288
00:12:38,258 --> 00:12:40,008
- I'll document with photos.
- Okay.

289
00:12:40,051 --> 00:12:41,969
Dana will finish up her work,
and I will be in the ER

290
00:12:42,053 --> 00:12:43,637
if you have any questions.

291
00:12:43,721 --> 00:12:45,181
You're in great hands.

292
00:12:45,265 --> 00:12:47,808
Thank you.

293
00:12:47,892 --> 00:12:50,144
All right, Ilana.

294
00:12:50,228 --> 00:12:52,146
I read your intake.

295
00:12:52,230 --> 00:12:53,480
Why don't you give me
your description

296
00:12:53,564 --> 00:12:54,983
of exactly what happened?

297
00:12:58,069 --> 00:13:02,031
I was at
a 4th of July barbecue

298
00:13:02,115 --> 00:13:04,825
with a bunch of friends.

299
00:13:04,909 --> 00:13:07,620
I helped set up.

300
00:13:07,704 --> 00:13:09,163
[Sniffles]

301
00:13:15,086 --> 00:13:16,629
Where does it hurt?

302
00:13:16,713 --> 00:13:20,132
<i>Like here,
under my belly button.</i>

303
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:23,510
Okay, do you have any fever,
vomiting, diarrhea?

304
00:13:23,594 --> 00:13:26,972
<i>- Oh, no.
It's--it's just a stomachache.</i>

305
00:13:27,056 --> 00:13:28,974
Okay, well, still, go see
the nurse and have her call me.

306
00:13:29,058 --> 00:13:30,684
<i>Okay.</i>

307
00:13:30,768 --> 00:13:33,145
<i>But I'm still having
ice cream tonight.</i>

308
00:13:33,229 --> 00:13:35,314
Why don't you see
how you feel later?

309
00:13:35,398 --> 00:13:38,734
<i>- It--it's not bad.
You don't have to get so sad.</i>

310
00:13:38,818 --> 00:13:41,111
- I'm not sad.
I'm--
- I'm good.

311
00:13:41,195 --> 00:13:43,364
<i>Your face doesn't look good.</i>

312
00:13:43,448 --> 00:13:44,949
Oh.

313
00:13:45,033 --> 00:13:47,034
Well, you still wanna watch
the fireworks tonight?

314
00:13:47,118 --> 00:13:48,244
[Siren whoops]
I have our headphones--

315
00:13:48,328 --> 00:13:49,954
[Speaking Tamil]

316
00:13:50,038 --> 00:13:52,540
- I'm not being rude.
- Sorry, Becca. I gotta go.

317
00:13:58,588 --> 00:14:01,715
Elliot Green, 17, syncopal
episode at football practice.

318
00:14:01,799 --> 00:14:03,634
Look, I just got dizzy, okay?

319
00:14:03,718 --> 00:14:05,094
It's hell week.
I need to get back.

320
00:14:05,178 --> 00:14:07,054
Yeah, okay, tough guy.

321
00:14:07,138 --> 00:14:10,933
A and O, systolic of 95, tachy
at 122, no meds, no allergies.

322
00:14:11,017 --> 00:14:12,567
How long were you
at practice?

323
00:14:12,643 --> 00:14:15,020
I started at 9:00,
so, like, four hours.

324
00:14:15,104 --> 00:14:17,398
Four hours in this heat
with all that gear?

325
00:14:17,482 --> 00:14:19,484
No pain, no game.

326
00:14:21,527 --> 00:14:23,988
God, I'm hungry.

327
00:14:25,823 --> 00:14:29,076
Hey. When's our break?
- There's no breaks down here.

328
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:32,037
Always make sure you pack
a protein bar, something quick.

329
00:14:32,121 --> 00:14:35,916
Ogilvie, Joy,
jump in on this.

330
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,459
Syncope at football practice.

331
00:14:37,543 --> 00:14:40,587
- No, I just--
I just needed to hydrate.

332
00:14:40,671 --> 00:14:42,006
Possible heatstroke?

333
00:14:42,090 --> 00:14:43,173
Well, with heatstroke,
you would have

334
00:14:43,257 --> 00:14:44,633
an altered mental status.

335
00:14:44,717 --> 00:14:46,135
And they're usually dry,
not sweaty.

336
00:14:46,219 --> 00:14:47,970
Mortality is 50%,
especially in the elderly.

337
00:14:48,054 --> 00:14:50,139
In extreme heat like this...

338
00:14:51,349 --> 00:14:52,849
Langdon, can you cover this?

339
00:14:52,850 --> 00:14:55,185
- No problem.
- Mr. Diaz. Orlando.

340
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:57,146
Orlando, where are you going?

341
00:14:57,230 --> 00:14:59,023
- Home. Can you take these out?
- Uh, no.

342
00:14:59,107 --> 00:15:01,108
It takes 48 hours for you
to get out of DKA.

343
00:15:01,192 --> 00:15:02,943
Your blood is still
full of acid.

344
00:15:03,027 --> 00:15:04,445
Look, I can't add
thousands of dollars

345
00:15:04,529 --> 00:15:05,779
to the 100 grand I already owe.

346
00:15:05,863 --> 00:15:07,698
- I'm--
- I'm sorry.
100 grand?

347
00:15:07,782 --> 00:15:09,982
- In medical debt.
My wife doesn't even know.

348
00:15:10,034 --> 00:15:11,952
I'll never be able
to pay it off as it is.

349
00:15:12,036 --> 00:15:13,120
Where are your wife
and daughter?

350
00:15:13,204 --> 00:15:14,663
Maybe we can all talk.

351
00:15:14,747 --> 00:15:16,290
I told them to go back
to work a couple hours ago.

352
00:15:16,374 --> 00:15:17,916
But the hospital is
giving you a big discount.

353
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:19,668
And, Mr. Diaz,
I know it's not ideal,

354
00:15:19,752 --> 00:15:21,462
but can you stay
for at least 12 hours?

355
00:15:21,546 --> 00:15:23,088
It would get you out
of the danger zone.

356
00:15:23,172 --> 00:15:25,799
No. I really can't.

357
00:15:25,883 --> 00:15:29,178
Every minute I stay is a meal,
shoes, school supplies.

358
00:15:29,262 --> 00:15:31,762
Plus, I have a second job
I have to get to by 4:00.

359
00:15:31,764 --> 00:15:34,683
- You need fluids!
- I drink plenty of water.

360
00:15:34,767 --> 00:15:37,102
- And potassium and insulin.
Okay, how about this?

361
00:15:37,186 --> 00:15:39,813
You stay and I'll get together
everything you'll need at home.

362
00:15:39,897 --> 00:15:44,026
Also, a referral to Northside
Christian Health Center.

363
00:15:44,110 --> 00:15:46,487
Come on.
You don't work until 4:00.

364
00:15:46,571 --> 00:15:49,021
It'll keep you from passing out
on the job again--

365
00:15:49,073 --> 00:15:50,283
Or worse.

366
00:15:54,328 --> 00:15:55,746
Okay, I guess.

367
00:15:55,830 --> 00:15:56,997
Great.

368
00:15:57,081 --> 00:15:58,832
Thank you. Please.

369
00:15:58,916 --> 00:16:01,294
[Sighs]

370
00:16:02,253 --> 00:16:03,962
Sats up to 98.

371
00:16:04,046 --> 00:16:06,548
- Neonatal mask is working.
- Santos, finish the FAST.

372
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:07,758
What--what are
you injecting?

373
00:16:07,842 --> 00:16:09,176
Lido with epi.

374
00:16:09,260 --> 00:16:10,636
It'll clamp off
any little bleeders.

375
00:16:10,720 --> 00:16:12,221
- We need some skin hooks.
Four Shiley?

376
00:16:12,305 --> 00:16:14,556
Mm, I don't like
the curve of a Shiley.

377
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:16,141
I didn't know
you were so picky.

378
00:16:16,225 --> 00:16:17,309
Santos, take a break.

379
00:16:17,393 --> 00:16:19,353
Help me cut down a 6-0 ET tube.

380
00:16:19,437 --> 00:16:20,854
What is going on here?

381
00:16:20,938 --> 00:16:22,481
You have a field medic
assisting you?

382
00:16:22,565 --> 00:16:23,857
Dr. Abbot is an attending,

383
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:25,526
and he's also a SWAT physician.

384
00:16:25,610 --> 00:16:28,654
My buddy Hiro here
is in bad need of an airway.

385
00:16:28,738 --> 00:16:29,905
Cut it right here.
- We can do this.

386
00:16:29,989 --> 00:16:31,240
No, no, I got it.

387
00:16:31,324 --> 00:16:32,366
You must be Gloria's new hire.

388
00:16:32,450 --> 00:16:33,992
Yes. Dr. Al-Hashimi.

389
00:16:34,076 --> 00:16:36,078
Well, I'd shake your hand,
but my tube is ready.

390
00:16:36,162 --> 00:16:37,746
And if I could find
and secure the distal trachea,

391
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:39,206
we have a shot at this.

392
00:16:39,290 --> 00:16:41,583
Okay, keeping
an eye on the sats.

393
00:16:41,667 --> 00:16:43,836
- Slow is smooth.
Smooth is fast.

394
00:16:43,920 --> 00:16:46,046
You know, you can call me
just to say hi sometimes.

395
00:16:46,130 --> 00:16:47,381
What's up now?

396
00:16:47,465 --> 00:16:49,015
GSW with tracheal
transection.

397
00:16:49,050 --> 00:16:52,386
Very retracted,
but I think I can get it.

398
00:16:52,470 --> 00:16:54,096
- Both lungs are up?
[Monitor beeping]

399
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:56,330
- Sats down to 91.
- Scanning the belly now.

400
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:57,850
Okay.

401
00:16:59,519 --> 00:17:01,145
I got it. I got it.

402
00:17:04,273 --> 00:17:06,066
Gently, gently,
or we're gonna lose it.

403
00:17:06,150 --> 00:17:07,901
Down to 89.

404
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:09,069
Oh, no.

405
00:17:09,153 --> 00:17:11,030
I'm in. Balloon up.

406
00:17:13,157 --> 00:17:15,742
End tidal,
excellent wave form.

407
00:17:15,826 --> 00:17:18,036
Good breath sounds.

408
00:17:18,120 --> 00:17:21,415
I'll sew the tracheal
to the skin, 2-0 silk.

409
00:17:21,499 --> 00:17:23,125
- Sats are coming up.
- Whoo.

410
00:17:23,209 --> 00:17:25,711
Not bad, Abbot.
- [Exhales]

411
00:17:25,795 --> 00:17:27,796
Mm, while you were playing
with that airway,

412
00:17:27,880 --> 00:17:29,798
you missed a big bruise
in the left upper quadrant.

413
00:17:29,882 --> 00:17:31,282
He was wearing body armor.

414
00:17:31,342 --> 00:17:32,426
High-velocity projectile
doesn't have

415
00:17:32,510 --> 00:17:34,595
to penetrate to damage.

416
00:17:34,679 --> 00:17:36,930
There's no fluid
in the suprasplenic space.

417
00:17:37,014 --> 00:17:39,099
Let me look.

418
00:17:39,183 --> 00:17:40,351
Okay, right there.

419
00:17:42,853 --> 00:17:45,105
Looks like a subcapsular
hematoma of his spleen.

420
00:17:45,189 --> 00:17:46,732
Must have been a big impact.

421
00:17:46,816 --> 00:17:49,485
AR-15 muzzle velocity
is 3,000 feet per second.

422
00:17:49,569 --> 00:17:51,111
CT angio of the neck ASAP,

423
00:17:51,195 --> 00:17:53,697
along with CT chest,
abdomen, pelvis.

424
00:17:53,781 --> 00:17:56,742
Yep, just as soon
as we secure this tube.

425
00:18:00,538 --> 00:18:02,956
- First liter's in.
- Mucous membranes dry.

426
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:05,125
Pupils four millimeters
reactive.

427
00:18:05,209 --> 00:18:06,502
Did you get tackled today?

428
00:18:06,586 --> 00:18:07,961
No, just running drills.

429
00:18:08,045 --> 00:18:09,796
- Any chest pain?
Palpitations?

430
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:11,256
No.

431
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:12,508
Hands off, please,
running the 12 lead.

432
00:18:12,592 --> 00:18:14,051
How are we looking?

433
00:18:14,135 --> 00:18:15,677
Good. Healthy kid.

434
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:17,304
No history, no trauma.

435
00:18:17,388 --> 00:18:20,182
Differential for syncope
in an adolescent?

436
00:18:20,266 --> 00:18:22,351
Cardiac arrhythmia
from drugs...

437
00:18:22,435 --> 00:18:23,519
- Hypovolemia, seizure...
- Long QT, WPW...

438
00:18:23,603 --> 00:18:25,270
- Sepsis.
- Or Brugada.

439
00:18:25,354 --> 00:18:27,504
Uh, Brugada is more
common in Asian males.

440
00:18:27,565 --> 00:18:28,941
But still
should be considered.

441
00:18:29,025 --> 00:18:30,609
Long odds, though.

442
00:18:30,693 --> 00:18:32,486
Brugada prevalence is
one in 20,000 in North America,

443
00:18:32,570 --> 00:18:35,155
as high as one in 300 in Asia
and the Middle East.

444
00:18:35,239 --> 00:18:36,657
And?

445
00:18:36,741 --> 00:18:38,867
First described in 1992,
has a high incidence

446
00:18:38,951 --> 00:18:40,661
of sudden death among
young patients with otherwise

447
00:18:40,745 --> 00:18:43,163
structurally normal hearts--
- Oof, oof, wait.

448
00:18:43,247 --> 00:18:44,665
Did you just say
"sudden death"?

449
00:18:44,749 --> 00:18:46,291
Temp is 102.5.

450
00:18:46,375 --> 00:18:47,668
Sorry, our student doctors
are discussing

451
00:18:47,752 --> 00:18:50,170
a rare condition
you don't have.

452
00:18:50,254 --> 00:18:53,257
- I--
- I just didn't
drink enough water.

453
00:18:53,341 --> 00:18:56,260
I overheated.

454
00:18:56,344 --> 00:18:58,011
Not my type, bud.

455
00:18:58,095 --> 00:19:00,973
Other than standard labs,
what else to order?

456
00:19:04,602 --> 00:19:06,395
CK to rule out rhabdo.

457
00:19:06,479 --> 00:19:07,688
To make sure you don't have

458
00:19:07,772 --> 00:19:09,231
any muscle breakdown
from the heat.

459
00:19:09,315 --> 00:19:11,400
Let's set up a cooling room
for Elliot here

460
00:19:11,484 --> 00:19:14,487
and the other heat exhaustions
we'll inevitably get today.

461
00:19:18,282 --> 00:19:19,950
Last photo.

462
00:19:20,034 --> 00:19:21,827
[Camera shutter clicks]

463
00:19:23,954 --> 00:19:25,163
Okay.

464
00:19:25,247 --> 00:19:27,416
We'll take the SD card
and seal it

465
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:30,544
in an evidence envelope
with everything else.

466
00:19:30,628 --> 00:19:32,045
Okay.

467
00:19:32,129 --> 00:19:36,049
Next, Emma's gonna
turn off the light,

468
00:19:36,133 --> 00:19:38,594
and I'll run a blue light
over your skin.

469
00:19:38,678 --> 00:19:44,057
Anything glows, I'll swab it
with a wet, then dry Q-tip.

470
00:19:44,141 --> 00:19:45,267
Is that okay?

471
00:19:45,351 --> 00:19:46,394
Yeah, sure.

472
00:19:48,979 --> 00:19:50,230
All right.

473
00:19:50,314 --> 00:19:52,441
Take off your gown
on the left side

474
00:19:52,525 --> 00:19:55,025
and turn a little bit
towards me, just to the left.

475
00:19:56,904 --> 00:19:58,280
There.

476
00:20:23,013 --> 00:20:24,556
Something on the left wrist.

477
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:25,725
Swab.

478
00:20:29,729 --> 00:20:33,106
[Sighs deeply]

479
00:20:33,190 --> 00:20:34,149
Sorry.

480
00:20:34,233 --> 00:20:35,567
Don't be.

481
00:20:35,651 --> 00:20:37,277
- It's just cold.
- Yeah.

482
00:20:37,361 --> 00:20:39,029
Almost done.

483
00:20:41,031 --> 00:20:43,075
[Beeping]

484
00:20:45,536 --> 00:20:47,746
- Thanks, Antoine.
- No problem.

485
00:20:47,830 --> 00:20:49,330
Keep your head down out there.

486
00:20:49,373 --> 00:20:50,957
What's the story?

487
00:20:51,041 --> 00:20:52,501
Neck angio is negative,
missed the carotids.

488
00:20:52,585 --> 00:20:54,419
- He's lucky.
- What about the belly?

489
00:20:54,503 --> 00:20:57,214
Small splenic injury,
no free fluid in the abdomen.

490
00:20:57,298 --> 00:20:59,049
- That should heal on its own.
- What's the plan?

491
00:20:59,133 --> 00:21:00,467
Head and Neck will have
an OR ready

492
00:21:00,551 --> 00:21:01,851
with thoracic standing by.

493
00:21:01,886 --> 00:21:03,595
How soon can they take him?

494
00:21:03,679 --> 00:21:04,971
We're a little backed up
with Westbridge patients,

495
00:21:05,055 --> 00:21:06,348
but let's bring him up.

496
00:21:06,432 --> 00:21:08,684
I'll get him
taken care of for you.

497
00:21:08,768 --> 00:21:10,560
Hey.

498
00:21:10,644 --> 00:21:13,647
You're gonna be okay, Hiro.
We're getting you to surgery.

499
00:21:13,731 --> 00:21:14,648
I'll write
the procedure note.

500
00:21:14,732 --> 00:21:15,775
Thank you.

501
00:21:20,905 --> 00:21:21,905
SWAT? Really?

502
00:21:21,989 --> 00:21:24,032
I suck at golf.

503
00:21:24,116 --> 00:21:26,326
You spend time
in the Middle East?

504
00:21:26,410 --> 00:21:28,036
More than I would have liked.

505
00:21:28,120 --> 00:21:30,831
I worked in Kabul
with Médecins Sans Frontières

506
00:21:30,915 --> 00:21:33,625
and in 2020,
at the maternity hospital.

507
00:21:33,709 --> 00:21:37,212
I met the most incredible,
bravest doctors there.

508
00:21:37,296 --> 00:21:39,506
Dasht-e-Barchi.

509
00:21:39,590 --> 00:21:42,300
Tragedy.

510
00:21:42,384 --> 00:21:45,345
We should grab a beer sometime,
share war stories.

511
00:21:45,429 --> 00:21:47,431
I'd like that.

512
00:21:50,559 --> 00:21:51,476
She seems cool.

513
00:21:51,560 --> 00:21:53,186
Yep, maybe.

514
00:21:53,270 --> 00:21:56,815
I'm not gonna be around
long enough to find out.

515
00:21:56,899 --> 00:21:58,942
Oh, there she is! Vic!

516
00:21:59,026 --> 00:22:00,235
Dad!

517
00:22:00,319 --> 00:22:03,530
Victoria,
this is Dr. Amy Joon.

518
00:22:03,614 --> 00:22:05,407
Dr. Joon is the smartest
person I know.

519
00:22:05,491 --> 00:22:06,700
Don't tell your mother.
Just kidding.

520
00:22:06,784 --> 00:22:08,076
[Laughs]

521
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:09,119
But seriously, don't.

522
00:22:09,203 --> 00:22:10,537
- [Laughs] Hi.
- Hello.

523
00:22:10,621 --> 00:22:12,706
Are--are you here
to see a patient?

524
00:22:12,790 --> 00:22:14,291
- No.
We're here to see you.

525
00:22:14,375 --> 00:22:15,709
Dr. Joon is Chief
of Dermatology.

526
00:22:15,793 --> 00:22:17,294
And Victoria's first
shift in the ER

527
00:22:17,378 --> 00:22:20,213
was on the day
of the PittFest shooting.

528
00:22:20,297 --> 00:22:22,299
I heard all
the incredible stories,

529
00:22:22,383 --> 00:22:26,136
including your own acts
of med student prowess.

530
00:22:26,220 --> 00:22:27,888
Wow, med student prowess.

531
00:22:27,972 --> 00:22:30,056
That's--[laughs]
I'm--
- I'm pretty sure

532
00:22:30,140 --> 00:22:31,683
I was just trying
to stay out of the way.

533
00:22:31,767 --> 00:22:32,934
Ah, she's modest,
like her dad.

534
00:22:33,018 --> 00:22:34,686
- And her mother?
[Phone rings]

535
00:22:34,770 --> 00:22:36,897
Oh. Sorry.

536
00:22:36,981 --> 00:22:38,732
Dr. Joon.

537
00:22:38,816 --> 00:22:40,776
Yep, coming.

538
00:22:40,860 --> 00:22:42,861
I'm doing a favor for someone
at the mayor's office

539
00:22:42,945 --> 00:22:45,739
who needs Mohs surgery
on a basal cell carcinoma.

540
00:22:45,823 --> 00:22:47,741
And then I am grilling for 30.

541
00:22:47,825 --> 00:22:49,743
- Oh, wow.
- Happy 4th, all.

542
00:22:49,827 --> 00:22:51,077
- Happy 4th.
- Yeah. [laughs]

543
00:22:51,161 --> 00:22:53,288
- Thanks for coming down.
- My pleasure.

544
00:22:53,372 --> 00:22:55,373
Let's grab a coffee sometime.
- Absolutely. Yes.

545
00:22:55,457 --> 00:22:57,876
Thank you.

546
00:22:57,960 --> 00:23:00,310
You know Mom really wants me
to go into surgery.

547
00:23:00,379 --> 00:23:02,329
Ah, your mom wants me
to stop drinking

548
00:23:02,339 --> 00:23:04,591
and join a pickleball league.
- Oh, that's the same.

549
00:23:04,675 --> 00:23:06,301
- Yeah, well--
- Exact same.

550
00:23:06,385 --> 00:23:08,762
I will risk an Achilles tear
before I give up scotch.

551
00:23:08,846 --> 00:23:10,597
[Chuckles] Hey, I hope I didn't
embarrass you coming down here.

552
00:23:10,681 --> 00:23:12,182
No.

553
00:23:12,266 --> 00:23:13,809
I'm just trying to present
you with some options

554
00:23:13,893 --> 00:23:15,435
for your residency.

555
00:23:15,519 --> 00:23:17,354
- I--
- I really
appreciate it, Dad.

556
00:23:17,438 --> 00:23:19,606
I do.
I just--

557
00:23:19,690 --> 00:23:21,775
I'm still not sure.

558
00:23:21,859 --> 00:23:23,443
Well, either way,
you'll do what's right.

559
00:23:23,527 --> 00:23:24,778
You always do.

560
00:23:24,862 --> 00:23:26,780
Proud of ya.
- Okay.

561
00:23:26,864 --> 00:23:29,366
Dr. Javadi, you are
a man of many talents.

562
00:23:29,450 --> 00:23:31,117
- [Laughs]
You don't know the half of it.

563
00:23:31,201 --> 00:23:32,285
- [Chuckles]
Your daughter has some

564
00:23:32,369 --> 00:23:33,912
high standards to live up to.

565
00:23:33,996 --> 00:23:36,540
Oh, you don't know
the half of it.

566
00:23:39,710 --> 00:23:42,838
Mr. and Mrs. Davis, this is
Dr. Jefferson from Psychiatry.

567
00:23:42,922 --> 00:23:44,840
Please call me Caleb.

568
00:23:44,924 --> 00:23:47,300
Can you tell us what's
going on with our son?

569
00:23:47,384 --> 00:23:51,137
All of his labs
and X-rays came back normal.

570
00:23:51,221 --> 00:23:54,850
Given his age
and his hearing voices,

571
00:23:54,934 --> 00:23:59,354
do either of you have a family
history of mental illness?

572
00:23:59,438 --> 00:24:00,773
Not mine.

573
00:24:05,152 --> 00:24:07,654
[Clears throat]

574
00:24:07,738 --> 00:24:09,322
My brother took his own life.

575
00:24:09,406 --> 00:24:11,658
Wait, what?

576
00:24:11,742 --> 00:24:13,994
Uncle Ken?

577
00:24:14,078 --> 00:24:15,829
You said he drank
himself to death.

578
00:24:15,913 --> 00:24:17,664
Ma.
- He did that too.

579
00:24:17,748 --> 00:24:18,957
Was he ever
formally diagnosed

580
00:24:19,041 --> 00:24:20,041
with a mental health issue?

581
00:24:20,125 --> 00:24:21,501
No.

582
00:24:21,585 --> 00:24:24,629
He was depressed,
had mood swings.

583
00:24:24,713 --> 00:24:26,381
But he didn't wanna see anyone.
- Oh, my God.

584
00:24:26,465 --> 00:24:28,565
Okay, why am I just now
hearing about this?

585
00:24:28,592 --> 00:24:30,927
- Jada, please.
- Please what, Mom?

586
00:24:31,011 --> 00:24:33,847
Why would you not
tell Jackson or me?

587
00:24:33,931 --> 00:24:35,381
[Scoffs]
I can't believe this.

588
00:24:35,391 --> 00:24:36,975
- Jada.
- Excuse me.

589
00:24:37,059 --> 00:24:38,102
Jada.

590
00:24:45,776 --> 00:24:47,694
What happens next?

591
00:24:47,778 --> 00:24:49,988
We keep your son here
for the next three days

592
00:24:50,072 --> 00:24:52,073
for observation and therapy.

593
00:24:52,157 --> 00:24:54,576
And that will help us
to understand what is going on.

594
00:24:54,660 --> 00:24:56,210
Jada should really hear this.

595
00:24:56,286 --> 00:24:58,831
Let me see if I can find her,
bring her back.

596
00:25:01,792 --> 00:25:04,044
- Okay.
I'm gonna swab your mouth now.

597
00:25:04,128 --> 00:25:05,879
My mouth?

598
00:25:05,963 --> 00:25:09,758
Two dry swabs along
the inside of your cheek

599
00:25:09,842 --> 00:25:11,760
and then along the gum line.

600
00:25:15,556 --> 00:25:17,433
How you feeling?

601
00:25:19,309 --> 00:25:21,269
I wish this day
never happened.

602
00:25:21,353 --> 00:25:23,271
Would you like some medicine
to help you relax?

603
00:25:23,355 --> 00:25:25,315
You've experienced
a horrific trauma.

604
00:25:28,027 --> 00:25:29,903
You've been
doing this a while?

605
00:25:29,987 --> 00:25:31,237
Let's just say
Florence Nightingale

606
00:25:31,321 --> 00:25:33,281
and I were roommates.

607
00:25:33,365 --> 00:25:35,784
- Who?
- [Chuckles]

608
00:25:35,868 --> 00:25:37,452
I rest my case.

609
00:25:37,536 --> 00:25:39,580
She was the founder
of modern nursing.

610
00:25:41,790 --> 00:25:43,959
Okay, you can have something
to eat or drink now.

611
00:25:44,043 --> 00:25:45,961
- I'm fine.
- Are you sure?

612
00:25:46,045 --> 00:25:47,712
I'll just keep going.

613
00:25:47,796 --> 00:25:49,673
Okay.

614
00:25:56,680 --> 00:26:01,267
We now have a heat exhaustion
treatment area in North five.

615
00:26:01,351 --> 00:26:03,770
- Evaporated cooling.
Great plan.

616
00:26:03,854 --> 00:26:08,650
Yeah, it was
Dr. Langdon's idea.

617
00:26:08,734 --> 00:26:12,320
He figured we'd be seeing a lot
more patients in this heat.

618
00:26:12,404 --> 00:26:14,114
He's right.

619
00:26:14,198 --> 00:26:15,365
How are you feeling?

620
00:26:15,449 --> 00:26:17,826
- [Sighs]
That's a loaded question.

621
00:26:17,910 --> 00:26:19,995
It wasn't meant to be.

622
00:26:20,079 --> 00:26:22,205
You have a deposition
in a couple of hours?

623
00:26:22,289 --> 00:26:24,457
- Yes.
- How are you feeling about it?

624
00:26:24,541 --> 00:26:26,459
Um, trying
to think positively

625
00:26:26,543 --> 00:26:29,671
but feeling, um, less so.

626
00:26:29,755 --> 00:26:31,881
This job's really important
to me and my sister.

627
00:26:31,965 --> 00:26:33,383
You know, I support both of us.

628
00:26:33,467 --> 00:26:34,567
It's gonna go great.

629
00:26:34,593 --> 00:26:36,302
Just tell them what happened.

630
00:26:36,386 --> 00:26:37,846
You're not at fault.
Your job's not in jeopardy.

631
00:26:37,930 --> 00:26:39,973
I mean, the lawyers
said that I could--

632
00:26:40,057 --> 00:26:42,142
The lawyers' job is to try
and shake your confidence.

633
00:26:42,226 --> 00:26:44,519
So don't let them.
You're a very good doctor.

634
00:26:44,603 --> 00:26:46,646
I have been training
residents for years.

635
00:26:46,730 --> 00:26:49,190
You are one of the very best.

636
00:26:49,274 --> 00:26:50,650
I am?

637
00:26:50,734 --> 00:26:51,776
No, we need
to stick to the plan.

638
00:26:51,860 --> 00:26:52,819
- I promise.
- Look.

639
00:26:52,903 --> 00:26:54,195
Thanks.

640
00:26:54,279 --> 00:26:55,488
She's not thinking
clearly, okay?

641
00:26:55,572 --> 00:26:56,672
It's gonna be great.

642
00:26:56,740 --> 00:26:57,991
This is not what she wants.

643
00:26:58,075 --> 00:26:59,826
Then I'm taking her home.
That's it.

644
00:26:59,910 --> 00:27:01,828
We have to honor
your wife's wishes.

645
00:27:01,912 --> 00:27:03,329
Even if she's
loaded up on morphine

646
00:27:03,413 --> 00:27:04,998
and can't think straight?
- Especially then.

647
00:27:05,082 --> 00:27:06,791
Hello.

648
00:27:06,875 --> 00:27:08,710
Paul Hamler, this is
my attending, Dr. Robinavitch.

649
00:27:08,794 --> 00:27:10,170
- Hi.
- Hi.

650
00:27:10,254 --> 00:27:12,672
Uh, my wife is not
thinking clearly.

651
00:27:12,756 --> 00:27:15,175
What is it that
she's asking for?

652
00:27:15,259 --> 00:27:17,427
Said she wants to stay here.

653
00:27:17,511 --> 00:27:19,304
Why don't we all
go in and talk?

654
00:27:20,764 --> 00:27:22,682
Brian Jenkins is
allowed to hunt with a .22

655
00:27:22,766 --> 00:27:24,267
on his grandpa's farm.

656
00:27:24,351 --> 00:27:26,269
Sounds like an accident
just waiting to happen.

657
00:27:26,353 --> 00:27:28,855
- Mm-hmm.
And you're not Brian Jenkins.

658
00:27:28,939 --> 00:27:31,441
How are we doing
in here, Roxie?

659
00:27:31,525 --> 00:27:33,193
Been better.

660
00:27:33,277 --> 00:27:34,736
Rumor has it
you're still interested

661
00:27:34,820 --> 00:27:37,197
in booking a room with us?

662
00:27:37,281 --> 00:27:39,365
I don't wanna
go back home yet.

663
00:27:39,449 --> 00:27:40,825
It's all set up, Rox.

664
00:27:40,909 --> 00:27:42,994
You're gonna be
more comfortable at home.

665
00:27:43,078 --> 00:27:45,205
Paul, I changed my mind.

666
00:27:45,289 --> 00:27:46,540
It is our home.

667
00:27:48,584 --> 00:27:50,502
I don't--

668
00:27:50,586 --> 00:27:52,337
I don't want you
living with my ghost.

669
00:27:52,421 --> 00:27:54,339
I will happily
live with your ghost.

670
00:27:54,423 --> 00:27:57,717
Can we just all stop
talking about ghosts, please?

671
00:27:57,801 --> 00:27:59,052
Yes. I'm sorry.

672
00:27:59,136 --> 00:28:01,846
I'm sorry, sweetie.
You're right.

673
00:28:01,930 --> 00:28:03,765
- Got trauma flying in.
ETA, five minutes.

674
00:28:03,849 --> 00:28:05,934
- Okay.
Um, I'm very sorry.

675
00:28:06,018 --> 00:28:07,393
I will be right back.

676
00:28:07,477 --> 00:28:09,938
Excuse me.

677
00:28:10,022 --> 00:28:12,148
It's a boating accident,
swimmer versus propeller.

678
00:28:12,232 --> 00:28:13,650
Ouch.

679
00:28:13,734 --> 00:28:15,235
What body parts involved?
- They didn't say.

680
00:28:15,319 --> 00:28:16,736
- How old?
- Nope.

681
00:28:16,820 --> 00:28:18,071
Anything?

682
00:28:18,155 --> 00:28:19,572
All I got was
boating accident,

683
00:28:19,656 --> 00:28:21,491
swimmer versus propeller.
- Propeller. Got it.

684
00:28:21,575 --> 00:28:23,035
[Elevator dings]

685
00:28:50,979 --> 00:28:52,397
[helicopter whirring]

686
00:28:52,481 --> 00:28:55,608
Picked a hell of a day
to come back, huh?

687
00:28:55,692 --> 00:28:58,611
How's Jake?

688
00:28:58,695 --> 00:29:00,405
He's good.

689
00:29:00,489 --> 00:29:02,615
He's better. He's coping.

690
00:29:02,699 --> 00:29:04,617
He's gonna be
a senior this fall.

691
00:29:04,701 --> 00:29:07,162
That's great.

692
00:29:07,246 --> 00:29:10,331
That was a lot
for him to go through.

693
00:29:10,415 --> 00:29:12,292
A lot for all of us
to go through.

694
00:29:12,376 --> 00:29:13,710
Yeah.

695
00:29:15,462 --> 00:29:17,380
Okay, I'm just gonna say it!

696
00:29:17,464 --> 00:29:18,882
I'm sorry.

697
00:29:18,966 --> 00:29:20,550
I betrayed your trust.

698
00:29:20,634 --> 00:29:22,510
I betrayed our patients' trust.

699
00:29:22,594 --> 00:29:23,887
And I'm really fucking sorry.

700
00:29:23,971 --> 00:29:26,181
It'll never happen again,
I swear.

701
00:29:30,602 --> 00:29:34,106
I'm really glad that you
got the help that you need.

702
00:29:36,858 --> 00:29:40,529
But I don't know if
I want you working in my ER.

703
00:29:47,119 --> 00:29:48,536
[Elevator dings]

704
00:29:48,620 --> 00:29:49,871
Why'd you intubate him?

705
00:29:49,955 --> 00:29:51,331
He was splinting
from the pain,

706
00:29:51,415 --> 00:29:52,874
barely moving air
with sats in the 80s.

707
00:29:52,958 --> 00:29:54,167
How'd he get sliced up
in the propeller?

708
00:29:54,251 --> 00:29:55,668
He was in the Allegheny

709
00:29:55,752 --> 00:29:57,045
trying to untangle
a water ski tow line

710
00:29:57,129 --> 00:29:58,046
when his buddy
started the engine.

711
00:29:58,130 --> 00:29:59,339
Drunk buddy, I assume?

712
00:29:59,423 --> 00:30:00,798
- Well, it's 4th of July.
You tell me.

713
00:30:00,882 --> 00:30:02,133
Focus on the patient, please.

714
00:30:02,217 --> 00:30:04,094
Sofie, take over bagging.

715
00:30:06,263 --> 00:30:08,348
Okay. One, two, three.

716
00:30:08,432 --> 00:30:09,433
Watch that buckle.

717
00:30:10,934 --> 00:30:12,227
- Do you need me in here?
- Nope.

718
00:30:12,311 --> 00:30:14,854
We have a senior resident
and an attending.

719
00:30:14,938 --> 00:30:16,189
Mel, can we start with a--

720
00:30:16,273 --> 00:30:18,691
- An EFAST? Sure.
- Yes, please.

721
00:30:18,775 --> 00:30:20,360
Why?

722
00:30:20,444 --> 00:30:21,736
To check and make sure
there's no pneumothorax.

723
00:30:21,820 --> 00:30:23,363
Otherwise, it could
become a tension.

724
00:30:23,447 --> 00:30:26,115
Exactly. Oh, wow.

725
00:30:26,199 --> 00:30:28,243
You want O-neg?
- Not without a BP first.

726
00:30:28,327 --> 00:30:31,454
108/64, pulse is 102.

727
00:30:31,538 --> 00:30:33,788
Sats are good.
- Okay, let's have O-neg ready,

728
00:30:33,790 --> 00:30:36,709
but don't give it just yet.
- Anything else?

729
00:30:36,793 --> 00:30:38,920
[Alarm blaring]

730
00:30:39,004 --> 00:30:40,505
How about a hemocue?

731
00:30:40,589 --> 00:30:42,632
- Uh, yeah.
Yeah, yeah, of course.

732
00:30:50,766 --> 00:30:52,392
Next step is fingernails.

733
00:30:54,311 --> 00:30:56,604
We'll go under each nail,

734
00:30:56,688 --> 00:31:00,942
first with the wet swab
and then with the dry one.

735
00:31:01,026 --> 00:31:03,403
Do you wanna take a break, hon?

736
00:31:03,487 --> 00:31:05,238
No.

737
00:31:08,325 --> 00:31:11,411
[Breathing shakily]
How much longer?

738
00:31:11,495 --> 00:31:13,079
After these,
we'll get to external...

739
00:31:13,163 --> 00:31:14,414
[Knock at door]

740
00:31:14,498 --> 00:31:16,208
And internal
vaginal collection.

741
00:31:19,836 --> 00:31:23,506
It's the advocate from PAAR.

742
00:31:23,590 --> 00:31:25,258
They've been doing this
longer than I have.

743
00:31:25,342 --> 00:31:27,510
They provide resources,
assistance, and support

744
00:31:27,594 --> 00:31:29,304
for sexual assault survivors.

745
00:31:31,515 --> 00:31:34,309
Hey.

746
00:31:34,393 --> 00:31:36,769
This will not define you, okay?

747
00:31:36,853 --> 00:31:40,440
You don't have to talk to them,
but I recommend you do.

748
00:31:40,524 --> 00:31:42,401
They're available 24/7.

749
00:31:44,277 --> 00:31:46,488
- Okay.
- Okay.

750
00:31:52,577 --> 00:31:54,412
Hi.

751
00:31:54,496 --> 00:31:56,622
I'm Paulette Sanderson from
Pittsburgh Action Against Rape.

752
00:31:56,706 --> 00:31:58,750
- Hi, Paulette.
I'm the SANE, Dana.

753
00:31:58,834 --> 00:32:00,835
And this is Ilana.
- Hello.

754
00:32:00,919 --> 00:32:03,421
I'm sorry to meet you
under these circumstances,

755
00:32:03,505 --> 00:32:05,423
but I and my organization
are here to help you navigate

756
00:32:05,507 --> 00:32:07,467
everything that comes next.

757
00:32:07,551 --> 00:32:10,511
I brought you some clothes
and basic necessities.

758
00:32:10,595 --> 00:32:12,138
I can even stay with you
through the rest

759
00:32:12,222 --> 00:32:14,307
of your examination
if you'd like.

760
00:32:16,601 --> 00:32:18,102
I don't think
that's necessary.

761
00:32:18,186 --> 00:32:20,688
- Okay.
- That's fine.

762
00:32:20,772 --> 00:32:23,316
Would it be okay if
I asked you a few questions?

763
00:32:33,785 --> 00:32:35,078
Sure.

764
00:32:35,162 --> 00:32:37,330
[Phone rings]

765
00:32:37,414 --> 00:32:40,833
Mm, our VRI isn't working.

766
00:32:40,917 --> 00:32:43,669
Video Relay Interpreter?

767
00:32:43,753 --> 00:32:45,253
Yeah, of course I rebooted it.

768
00:32:45,297 --> 00:32:46,839
Wait, how are you gonna
fix it if you don't know

769
00:32:46,923 --> 00:32:48,925
what the hell it is?

770
00:32:49,009 --> 00:32:51,177
Yeah, okay.
Whatever.

771
00:32:51,261 --> 00:32:53,179
I wanna do a head
and belly scan on Harlow.

772
00:32:53,263 --> 00:32:54,389
Can you try telling her why?

773
00:32:54,473 --> 00:32:55,640
What about the VRI?

774
00:32:55,724 --> 00:32:57,642
It's DOA.

775
00:32:57,726 --> 00:33:00,561
I'm charting every
free minute I get.

776
00:33:00,645 --> 00:33:02,397
I wasn't coming over
for that.

777
00:33:02,481 --> 00:33:04,149
Good job in the Trauma earlier.

778
00:33:07,402 --> 00:33:08,403
What's this?

779
00:33:08,487 --> 00:33:09,737
Daniel Scott, 32,

780
00:33:09,821 --> 00:33:11,489
weak and dizzy
while washing his car.

781
00:33:11,573 --> 00:33:13,991
Tachy at 106, BP 90/60.

782
00:33:14,075 --> 00:33:15,535
Temp's too high to register.

783
00:33:15,619 --> 00:33:17,161
We have a cooling room
set up in North five.

784
00:33:17,245 --> 00:33:18,246
Okay, how are you
feeling, Mr. Scott?

785
00:33:18,330 --> 00:33:19,539
Thirsty.

786
00:33:19,623 --> 00:33:20,998
Let's see if
we can't fix that.

787
00:33:21,082 --> 00:33:22,875
He's gonna need a core temp,
a CMP--whoa.

788
00:33:22,959 --> 00:33:24,377
Oh, hey, we need
a trauma room.

789
00:33:24,461 --> 00:33:25,586
What's open?
- Two.

790
00:33:25,670 --> 00:33:27,213
I'll grab the Ativan.

791
00:33:27,297 --> 00:33:28,897
- Any past medical history?
- No.

792
00:33:28,965 --> 00:33:30,633
Wife says he's healthy.
No meds, no allergies.

793
00:33:30,717 --> 00:33:33,345
He needs a core temp.

794
00:33:37,474 --> 00:33:38,975
Ready to transfer.

795
00:33:39,059 --> 00:33:40,309
Let's give two of Ativan.

796
00:33:40,352 --> 00:33:41,802
Don't want him seizing again.

797
00:33:41,853 --> 00:33:42,979
I gotta get back
to my patients.

798
00:33:43,063 --> 00:33:43,980
Okay.

799
00:33:44,064 --> 00:33:46,732
One, two, three.

800
00:33:46,816 --> 00:33:47,900
Orders?

801
00:33:47,984 --> 00:33:50,069
Second IV with saline open.

802
00:33:50,153 --> 00:33:53,406
Sepsis panel, UA,
urine drug screen, EKG, and CK.

803
00:33:53,490 --> 00:33:55,408
I don't see any
apparent trauma.

804
00:33:55,492 --> 00:33:56,909
[Alarms ringing]

805
00:33:56,993 --> 00:33:59,620
Pupils reactive.
- Mr. Scott? Daniel?

806
00:33:59,704 --> 00:34:01,289
Can you talk to me?

807
00:34:01,373 --> 00:34:02,957
Post-ictal,
but moving all extremities.

808
00:34:03,041 --> 00:34:04,959
Pulse 137, BP 88/60.

809
00:34:05,043 --> 00:34:06,627
What are you thinking,
Dr. Santos?

810
00:34:06,711 --> 00:34:09,548
Uh, heat stroke,
but consider sepsis or drugs.

811
00:34:13,134 --> 00:34:16,554
Rectal temp is 104.6.

812
00:34:16,638 --> 00:34:18,556
All right, let's start
with four ice packs

813
00:34:18,640 --> 00:34:20,391
on the groin and axilla.

814
00:34:20,475 --> 00:34:22,310
Should we do
a full body ice bath?

815
00:34:22,394 --> 00:34:23,603
- That'll take too long.
Do you have an Arctic Sun?

816
00:34:23,687 --> 00:34:25,104
Yeah, we do.

817
00:34:25,188 --> 00:34:26,689
Get pads on the chest,
abdomen, and both legs.

818
00:34:26,773 --> 00:34:28,275
I'll check back in.

819
00:34:30,068 --> 00:34:33,446
Ceftazidime is up,
and first hemoglobin, 8.2.

820
00:34:33,530 --> 00:34:36,199
- Eight is pretty low.
He must have bled down from 14.

821
00:34:36,283 --> 00:34:37,983
Anything you
wanna do about that?

822
00:34:38,034 --> 00:34:40,703
- Um, young, healthy guy.
We transfuse at seven.

823
00:34:40,787 --> 00:34:42,371
Do we?

824
00:34:42,455 --> 00:34:44,123
We'd be in real trouble
if he equilibrates

825
00:34:44,207 --> 00:34:46,292
from acute blood loss.
- Am I interrupting something?

826
00:34:46,376 --> 00:34:48,826
- Multiple deep lacerations--
- Motorboat versus--

827
00:34:51,381 --> 00:34:52,882
Jesus.

828
00:34:52,966 --> 00:34:54,550
This looks like some
"Jurassic Park" shit.

829
00:34:54,634 --> 00:34:56,636
Is that your official
surgical diagnosis?

830
00:34:56,720 --> 00:34:58,137
He is hemodynamically stable.

831
00:34:58,221 --> 00:35:00,640
What else do we know?

832
00:35:00,724 --> 00:35:04,310
Uh, intubated in the field
due to poor tidal volume.

833
00:35:04,394 --> 00:35:06,521
EFAST was negative
for pneumothorax,

834
00:35:06,605 --> 00:35:09,023
so no need to do a chest tube.

835
00:35:09,107 --> 00:35:11,776
And no free fluid
in the abdomen,

836
00:35:11,860 --> 00:35:13,510
good hemostasis
inside the wounds.

837
00:35:13,570 --> 00:35:14,987
Nothing arterial.

838
00:35:15,071 --> 00:35:16,614
At first, he had
a hemoglobin of 8.2.

839
00:35:16,698 --> 00:35:18,282
We'll follow that closely.

840
00:35:18,366 --> 00:35:21,066
With no active bleeding,
I wouldn't transfuse just yet.

841
00:35:23,246 --> 00:35:24,997
Dr. Langdon agrees with you.

842
00:35:25,081 --> 00:35:27,333
Let's get him to CT.

843
00:35:27,417 --> 00:35:29,752
Jason Stills, 62,
was gathering the makings

844
00:35:29,836 --> 00:35:32,338
of a salad when he started
feeling dizzy and nauseated.

845
00:35:32,422 --> 00:35:33,673
Vomited once.

846
00:35:33,757 --> 00:35:34,840
How are you feeling,
Mr. Stills?

847
00:35:34,924 --> 00:35:36,676
Like I'm gonna die.

848
00:35:36,760 --> 00:35:38,678
Well, you came to the right
place to prevent that.

849
00:35:38,762 --> 00:35:40,680
Do you mind
if I touch your abdomen?

850
00:35:40,764 --> 00:35:42,848
- Yeah, sure.
- Okay.

851
00:35:42,932 --> 00:35:45,268
Does this hurt at all?
- No.

852
00:35:45,352 --> 00:35:48,521
He's tachycardic at 124
with a temp of 102.4.

853
00:35:48,605 --> 00:35:50,523
Hey, Joy,
what's your suggestion?

854
00:35:50,607 --> 00:35:52,191
Keep hydrating,
check electrolytes,

855
00:35:52,275 --> 00:35:53,234
and move him
to the cooling room.

856
00:35:53,318 --> 00:35:54,527
Precisely.

857
00:35:54,611 --> 00:35:55,736
Good luck finding
a parking spot.

858
00:35:55,820 --> 00:35:58,698
- North five.
- What? No valet?

859
00:35:58,782 --> 00:36:00,116
[Elevator dings]

860
00:36:02,786 --> 00:36:04,579
Jada. Hey.

861
00:36:04,663 --> 00:36:06,706
I--I've been looking
all over for you.

862
00:36:06,790 --> 00:36:08,374
I just went for a walk.

863
00:36:08,458 --> 00:36:11,294
I wanted to talk to you,
if that's okay.

864
00:36:13,296 --> 00:36:15,214
So does Dr. Jefferson.

865
00:36:15,298 --> 00:36:17,383
It's important that you get
to hear what he has to say.

866
00:36:17,467 --> 00:36:18,843
Why?

867
00:36:18,927 --> 00:36:20,845
He doesn't want me to go crazy
like my brother?

868
00:36:20,929 --> 00:36:23,598
Or kill myself like my uncle?

869
00:36:23,682 --> 00:36:25,891
Of course not.

870
00:36:25,975 --> 00:36:28,725
We--we still have no idea
what caused Jackson's episode.

871
00:36:28,770 --> 00:36:31,272
- [Sighs]
Episode.

872
00:36:31,356 --> 00:36:33,566
Right.

873
00:36:33,650 --> 00:36:37,862
- Look, I--
- I know this
must be so scary for you.

874
00:36:37,946 --> 00:36:41,407
And you probably feel
betrayed by your parents.

875
00:36:41,491 --> 00:36:44,327
But they had no way
of knowing about Jackson.

876
00:36:44,411 --> 00:36:46,579
You know, and some families
just have a difficult time

877
00:36:46,663 --> 00:36:50,082
talking about mental health.

878
00:36:50,166 --> 00:36:52,126
Now you can help us
take the first steps

879
00:36:52,210 --> 00:36:55,338
to finding out what we can
do to help your brother.

880
00:37:00,677 --> 00:37:05,806
Mr. Diaz,
I have a surprise for you.

881
00:37:05,890 --> 00:37:07,642
Oh.

882
00:37:07,726 --> 00:37:08,934
Sorry.

883
00:37:09,018 --> 00:37:10,436
It's okay.

884
00:37:10,520 --> 00:37:12,320
Have you--have you
seen my patient?

885
00:37:12,355 --> 00:37:14,940
Orlando? Mr. Diaz?

886
00:37:15,024 --> 00:37:17,318
Room was empty.

887
00:37:17,402 --> 00:37:20,279
- Seriously?
- Yeah.

888
00:37:20,363 --> 00:37:21,865
[Sighs]

889
00:37:24,868 --> 00:37:26,452
What happened to you?

890
00:37:26,536 --> 00:37:28,412
Oh.

891
00:37:28,496 --> 00:37:29,789
Bullet grazed my vest.

892
00:37:29,873 --> 00:37:30,956
You were shot?

893
00:37:31,040 --> 00:37:32,833
Shot at.

894
00:37:32,917 --> 00:37:36,003
Geniuses thought today was the
day to rob a goods warehouse.

895
00:37:36,087 --> 00:37:37,171
Didn't think about
how long it would take

896
00:37:37,255 --> 00:37:38,506
to load the appliances.

897
00:37:38,590 --> 00:37:39,840
They panicked.

898
00:37:39,924 --> 00:37:41,050
All hell broke loose.

899
00:37:41,134 --> 00:37:42,802
Jesus.

900
00:37:45,263 --> 00:37:47,181
Why do you do this?

901
00:37:47,265 --> 00:37:49,225
My therapist said
I needed a hobby.

902
00:37:49,309 --> 00:37:50,893
Funny.

903
00:37:50,977 --> 00:37:52,978
[Sighs deeply]
Shit.

904
00:37:53,062 --> 00:37:55,189
This--this sucks.

905
00:37:55,273 --> 00:37:56,982
- Oh, it's nothing.
- No.

906
00:37:57,066 --> 00:37:59,193
- No, don't worry about me.
I'm fine. Seriously.

907
00:37:59,277 --> 00:38:00,486
No, my patient.

908
00:38:00,570 --> 00:38:02,279
He didn't have any insurance,

909
00:38:02,363 --> 00:38:06,534
and he was already
in a mountain of medical debt.

910
00:38:06,618 --> 00:38:08,369
He couldn't afford
any of his meds.

911
00:38:08,453 --> 00:38:10,788
Hmm.

912
00:38:10,872 --> 00:38:12,331
What's in the bag?

913
00:38:12,415 --> 00:38:17,294
Insulin, test strips,
electrolyte powder.

914
00:38:17,378 --> 00:38:20,005
I--I got him everything
he needed for home care.

915
00:38:20,089 --> 00:38:22,216
So Uber it to his house.

916
00:38:22,300 --> 00:38:24,552
Is the hospital
gonna pay for that?

917
00:38:24,636 --> 00:38:26,679
I'll pay for it.

918
00:38:36,856 --> 00:38:38,858
What are you doing?

919
00:38:38,942 --> 00:38:41,527
What you clearly can't.

920
00:38:41,611 --> 00:38:43,195
Did you make a chart?

921
00:38:43,279 --> 00:38:44,613
No.

922
00:38:44,697 --> 00:38:46,198
This can stay off the books.

923
00:38:46,282 --> 00:38:48,117
Don't need the paperwork
from the hospital

924
00:38:48,201 --> 00:38:49,910
or the police department.

925
00:38:49,994 --> 00:38:52,037
Okay.

926
00:38:52,121 --> 00:38:53,665
Our little secret.

927
00:38:57,293 --> 00:38:59,545
- How's he doing?
Any more seizures?

928
00:38:59,629 --> 00:39:00,713
Nope.

929
00:39:00,797 --> 00:39:02,047
Temp 102.9.

930
00:39:02,131 --> 00:39:03,382
Labs back?

931
00:39:03,466 --> 00:39:05,092
Mostly signs of dehydration.

932
00:39:05,176 --> 00:39:08,846
A tad hypernatremic,
mild BUN and creatinine bump.

933
00:39:08,930 --> 00:39:11,265
- CK 400 something--
Nothing worrisome yet.

934
00:39:11,349 --> 00:39:12,892
Okay, good. Keep cooling.

935
00:39:12,976 --> 00:39:14,935
- I'll monitor him.
- Great.

936
00:39:15,019 --> 00:39:17,856
That'll give Dr. Santos
a chance to get caught up.

937
00:39:21,442 --> 00:39:23,944
Your R2 year
can be challenging.

938
00:39:24,028 --> 00:39:26,906
You just have to keep grinding.

939
00:39:26,990 --> 00:39:28,908
What's your dispo plan
for Mr. Scott?

940
00:39:28,992 --> 00:39:30,910
Uh, ICU admission.

941
00:39:30,994 --> 00:39:32,912
You should call Neurology
to consult.

942
00:39:32,996 --> 00:39:34,705
Yeah, done.

943
00:39:34,789 --> 00:39:36,916
Since it was exertional heat
illness in a young person,

944
00:39:37,000 --> 00:39:38,793
the mortality is low.

945
00:39:38,877 --> 00:39:41,670
But non-exertional heatstroke
in an elderly person,

946
00:39:41,754 --> 00:39:43,756
you need to worry.
- Okay.

947
00:39:43,840 --> 00:39:46,759
I'll put in orders
for repeat labs.

948
00:39:46,843 --> 00:39:48,678
Good work in there.

949
00:39:54,934 --> 00:39:56,644
[Sighs]

950
00:40:01,900 --> 00:40:05,653
This 49-year-old woman presents
to the emergency department--

951
00:40:05,737 --> 00:40:08,948
[Baby wailing]

952
00:40:09,032 --> 00:40:13,619
Uh, with the chief complaint
of right ear pain.

953
00:40:13,703 --> 00:40:16,288
Hey, Donnie, can you do
something about that?

954
00:40:16,372 --> 00:40:17,748
What?

955
00:40:17,832 --> 00:40:19,291
Seriously?

956
00:40:19,375 --> 00:40:21,126
That--that's not
driving you nuts?

957
00:40:21,210 --> 00:40:23,254
The baby, it won't stop crying.

958
00:40:23,338 --> 00:40:25,256
- Oh, that?
It's music to my ears now.

959
00:40:25,340 --> 00:40:26,640
I think Jesse's the nurse.

960
00:40:26,716 --> 00:40:29,301
Well, can't you--ugh.

961
00:40:29,385 --> 00:40:32,430
[Baby continues wailing]

962
00:40:35,391 --> 00:40:36,559
Fuck.

963
00:40:41,731 --> 00:40:44,024
What the hell is going on?

964
00:40:44,108 --> 00:40:46,485
With what?

965
00:40:46,569 --> 00:40:49,530
- With her.
Can't you make her stop crying?

966
00:40:49,614 --> 00:40:52,514
- She's been fed and changed.
She's cranky from rhinovirus.

967
00:40:52,575 --> 00:40:54,159
[Baby wailing]

968
00:40:54,243 --> 00:40:56,495
Isn't there something
that you can do?

969
00:40:56,579 --> 00:40:59,081
She's due
for her next Tylenol.

970
00:40:59,165 --> 00:41:00,499
Give me a minute.
I'll be right back.

971
00:41:00,583 --> 00:41:02,733
Wait, no, no, no,
I'm not gonna stay here.

972
00:41:02,752 --> 00:41:05,379
[Wailing continues]

973
00:41:05,463 --> 00:41:07,340
What is your problem?

974
00:41:10,301 --> 00:41:14,471
This is precisely why
I didn't go into Pedes.

975
00:41:14,555 --> 00:41:15,639
Okay.

976
00:41:15,723 --> 00:41:17,558
Hey, hey.

977
00:41:17,642 --> 00:41:20,603
Hey, little Miss Sunshine.

978
00:41:22,271 --> 00:41:24,523
Is it time for you
to take a little nap?

979
00:41:24,607 --> 00:41:26,650
That would be so fucking nice.

980
00:41:26,734 --> 00:41:28,027
Yes, it would.

981
00:41:28,111 --> 00:41:29,695
[Baby wailing]

982
00:41:29,779 --> 00:41:31,322
[sighs]

983
00:41:31,406 --> 00:41:34,366
I'm starting to understand
why you got left here.

984
00:41:34,450 --> 00:41:36,536
Hey, shh.

985
00:41:38,579 --> 00:41:41,582
[Singing in Tagalog]

986
00:41:48,131 --> 00:41:50,550
[baby quieting]

987
00:42:09,193 --> 00:42:12,238
[humming]

988
00:42:22,957 --> 00:42:24,583
What's the word from CT?

989
00:42:24,667 --> 00:42:27,586
Nothing intrathoracic,
nothing intra-abdominal.

990
00:42:27,670 --> 00:42:28,921
Propeller just
missed gutting him.

991
00:42:29,005 --> 00:42:30,381
- Very fortunate.
- Okay.

992
00:42:30,465 --> 00:42:32,299
Repeat hemoglobin is eight.

993
00:42:32,383 --> 00:42:34,927
We're holding off
on transfusing.

994
00:42:35,011 --> 00:42:36,762
Plan?

995
00:42:36,846 --> 00:42:38,806
I'll have Mel and Langdon
suture up the lacerations.

996
00:42:38,890 --> 00:42:40,933
- Wait, what?
That could take days.

997
00:42:41,017 --> 00:42:42,393
I--I can't--

998
00:42:42,477 --> 00:42:44,353
- Calm down, Sadness.
I'm kidding.

999
00:42:44,437 --> 00:42:46,814
This is one for my skilled
surgical residents upstairs,

1000
00:42:46,898 --> 00:42:48,315
not you Boy Scout butchers.

1001
00:42:48,399 --> 00:42:49,699
Boy, I missed you, Yoyo.

1002
00:42:49,776 --> 00:42:52,027
Mm. Can't say the same.

1003
00:42:52,111 --> 00:42:55,447
Okay, let's take up
this art project.

1004
00:42:55,531 --> 00:42:56,782
So about before--

1005
00:42:56,866 --> 00:42:58,826
Back to it.

1006
00:42:58,910 --> 00:43:00,285
Good talk.

1007
00:43:00,369 --> 00:43:01,829
How we doing, Princess?

1008
00:43:01,913 --> 00:43:03,497
- All right.
A little bloated.

1009
00:43:03,581 --> 00:43:06,834
I had one too many hot dogs
from the truck.

1010
00:43:06,918 --> 00:43:09,003
You meant the board, huh?

1011
00:43:09,087 --> 00:43:12,131
Gus, our incarcerated patient,
got a spot upstairs.

1012
00:43:12,215 --> 00:43:15,759
Looking for our unhoused
patient, Digby, and, of course,

1013
00:43:15,843 --> 00:43:18,679
we have Whitaker, Donahue,
and the med students

1014
00:43:18,763 --> 00:43:21,413
on these diversion intakes,
but they just keep coming.

1015
00:43:21,432 --> 00:43:23,267
Yeah, we may need to start
just sending people up

1016
00:43:23,351 --> 00:43:25,477
and ask for forgiveness
instead of permission.

1017
00:43:25,561 --> 00:43:27,938
[Phone rings]
- Hello?

1018
00:43:28,022 --> 00:43:30,315
Oh, okay.

1019
